    {
      "id": "s003",
      "title": "Honest arithmetic",
      "text": "First, let us do the arithmetic honestly. Imagine a coffee that costs four dollars, bought every day for three hundred and sixty five days. Four times three hundred and sixty five is one thousand four hundred and sixty dollars. That is an illustrative example, not a claim about your spending. Your price, schedule, and choices could make the real number quite different.",
