    {
      "id": "s004",
      "title": "Gross versus net",
      "text": "And that total is not automatically money you can recover. If you make coffee at home instead, the beans, milk, and other supplies still cost something. The useful comparison is the difference between the two choices. If the alternative costs one dollar a day, the difference is three dollars, or one thousand and ninety five dollars across that same illustrative year.",
      "settings": {
