    {
      "id": "s005",
      "title": "Opportunity cost",
      "text": "That difference has an opportunity cost. In plain English, choosing one thing means giving up the next best thing you could have done with the same money. That might be a small emergency cushion, less debt, a weekend away, or something you value today. We do not need a predicted investment return to understand the trade. We just need an honest alternative.",
      "settings": {
        "space": "Qwen/Qwen3-TTS",
        "endpoint": "/generate_voice_clone",
        "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base",
        "model_size": "1.7B",
        "language": "English",
        "use_xvector_only": true,
        "reference": "Audio/ren_reference.wav",
        "transcript": "Audio/ren_reference.txt",
        "other_generation_parameters": "unchanged public Space defaults",
        "reference_sha256": "78de4bd45743554f15ce32d8db39deaf1c0b1a9a5cd69fabb6d637dff323ed1c",
        "transcript_sha256": "46de9b48af8de666aa7275169f1f95fab8a398de3198c7d2fa51edbe22fb8451"
      },
      "fingerprint": "a8ac72b41de4e642a5cb8b1920f52bd5ed9b3102d59b8b3e955dfe2d31cbf24e",
      "status": "pending",
      "attempts": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s006",
      "title": "Two people, different value",
      "text": "Picture two people making the same purchase. For Max, that coffee is ten quiet minutes before a demanding shift. He looks forward to it. For Lena, it is an automatic stop she barely notices, and sometimes she leaves half the cup untouched. The receipts look alike. The value does not. A sensible decision can be different for each of them without either person being irresponsible.",
      "settings": {
        "space": "Qwen/Qwen3-TTS",
        "endpoint": "/generate_voice_clone",
        "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base",
        "model_size": "1.7B",
        "language": "English",
        "use_xvector_only": true,
        "reference": "Audio/ren_reference.wav",
